90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 20 0 R
/E (The lower board was developed for the field line detection system \(Figure 10\). The assembly uses 32 LDR sensors combined with 32 red LEDs, responsible for the controlled illumination of the surface and the stability of the measurements. Each sensor and each light emitter has a dedicated resistor, totaling 64 resistors, ensuring the correct electrical operation of the circuit. Signal processing is performed by an ESP32-S3 microcontroller, responsible for the acquisition and processing of information. The readings are obtained through two CD74HC4067 multiplexers, allowing for expanded inputs and system organization. The identification of the markings is based on the difference in reflectance between the white of the lines and the green of the field, with the use of red LEDs to increase contrast. The processed information is then transmitted to the second ESP32-S3, located on the main board, where it is integrated into the overall control logic of the robot.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [69]
>>
endobj
