420 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 20 0 R
/E (The hyperbolic mirror, presented in Image 24, has a more specific geometry for image formation. In the tested configuration, the view obtained by the OpenMV, presented in Image 25, allowed the system to identify the ball and only one of the goals, the yellow goal. This limitation reduces the amount of information available simultaneously to the vision system.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [399]
>>
endobj
421 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 20 0 R
/E (The comparison demonstrated that, for the strategy developed by the team, the convex mirror presents a significant advantage. The ability to simultaneously visualize the ball and both goals allows the robot to have a complete reference of the field in real time, facilitating the selection of direction and actions during the match. Therefore, the convex mirror was selected for providing the most suitable visual coverage for the strategy, directly contributing to faster, continuous, and more efficient decision-making.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [400]
>>
endobj
422 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 20 0 R
/E (10.1 SCATTER PLOT)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [401]
>>
endobj
423 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 20 0 R
/E (The vision system uses the CIELAB color model \(Image 17\) to perform robust segmentation of field elements. Unlike spaces such as RGB, CIELAB separates luminance information \(L*\) from the chromatic components \(a* and b*\), allowing greater color detection stability under different lighting conditions. To ensure consistency, a white balance process is applied, correcting deviations caused by variations in ambient light. In addition, adjustments to the L* component are used to compensate for changes in brightness, maintaining reliability in color identification. As a result, detection, especially of elements such as the yellow goal, becomes more accurate and less sensitive to noise and external variations.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [402]
>>
endobj
424 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 20 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [403]
>>
endobj
425 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 20 0 R
/E (In the comparative analysis, an increase in the goal conversion rate, greater play repeatability, and a reduction in performance variations throughout the matches were observed. The 2026 season robot demonstrated more predictable behavior, greater operational stability, and a better ability to execute offensive actions with precision. Overall, the results demonstrate that the solutions adopted for 2026 not only mitigated limitations observed in 2025, but also significantly increased the level of offensive efficiency and goal-scoring accuracy of the system, consolidating a more robust, precise, and competitive architecture.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [404]
>>
endobj
